From: Aurelia contributors
Subject: Check demux seek failures and preserve valid stream positions

Propagate failed AVI navigation instead of parsing from the wrong position; retain
error results while reporting failed best-effort restores. Do not accept WebP/Targa
when their required seek fails. Reject an Ogg blind seek when no keyframe was found,
and keep the existing zero/error contract for short page reads while checking restore
failures. Validate signed NUV positions before unsigned comparisons, and calculate
AVI percentage positions without signedness mismatches or multiplication overflow.
Use typed byte arithmetic and bounded Annodex payload reads; remove unused skeleton
scan accumulators while keeping entry-count validation. Match MP4 unsigned sample
counts and reject a negative previous edit-list index before indexing its table.

